# Create a client at https://developer.audiotool.com/applications
# then copy this to .env and fill in your values.
#
# Redirect URL must include http://127.0.0.1:5173/ (or whatever port vite uses)
# The scope must be a subset of the scopes assigned to your app.
VITE_AUDIOTOOL_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_SAMPLE_SCOPE=project:write
#
# Step 16J global lookup: base URL of the deployed samplemap D1 worker.
# When set, the analysis pipeline reuses globally-known/compatible analyses
# instead of re-analyzing audio locally. When absent/empty, local analysis
# always runs (offline-first). This is NOT a secret.
# VITE_GLOBAL_WORKER_URL=https://samplemap-d1-worker.sumadmusic.workers.dev
#
# STEP82 — E2E-only: the DEDICATED, DISPOSABLE worker used by the live E2E test
# (e2e/global-population.spec.ts test 6), which performs real D1 WRITES. It is
# the same Worker implementation as production, bound to a SEPARATE D1 database
# via the `e2e` environment in workers/d1-worker/wrangler.toml.
#
# Test 6 FAILS LOUDLY when this is unset, and it also refuses the production
# URL — it never falls back. Set it in your shell before running the live E2E:
#   SAMPLEMAP_E2E_WORKER_URL=https://samplemap-d1-worker-e2e.sumadmusic.workers.dev \
#     npx playwright test e2e/global-population.spec.ts
# This is NOT a secret (no auth token is involved). Not a VITE_ var: it is read
# by the Playwright config/spec in Node, never shipped to the browser.
# SAMPLEMAP_E2E_WORKER_URL=https://samplemap-d1-worker-e2e.sumadmusic.workers.dev
